  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 230 AM EDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nConditions will remain wet and unsettled through the extended period \nas South Florida remains entrenched in an area of weakness between \ntwo ridges, and the upper level trough causing this weakness extends \nsouth across the Appalachian mountains. At the same time, some of \nthe ensemble suites are hinting at a few tropical upper tropospheric \ntroughs (TUTTs) meandering across the area, which could enhance \ninstability and lift and result in more widespread unsettled \nweather. In fact, the NBM is picking up on this possibility as we \nhead into the weekend, with Friday afternoon potentially being one of \nthe wetter ones this weekend (with 60-80% chances of rainfall), with \nactivity maximized across the interior and southwest portions of \nSouth Florida. With the potential for more widespread coverage, and \nthe added support from features aloft, the heavy rainfall could lead \nto localized flooding for portions of southwest FL. Temperatures \nwill remain in the low to mid 90s each afternoon. Ridging will start \nto build back and as we head into next week.",
